Skill Installer (Claude Code plugin)
Copyright 2026 Omer Yehuda

This plugin is adapted from the "skill-installer" system skill that ships with
OpenAI Codex (https://github.com/openai/skills), licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. A copy of that license is in LICENSE.

Changes from the original:
- Ported from Python to dependency-free Node.js and rewritten for Claude Code
  (installs into the user's or the project's Claude skills folder).
- Downloads one skill folder through the GitHub tree API and raw files instead
  of a whole-repo zip; hardened sparse git clone as the fallback (hooks off,
  symlinks off, no prompts).
- New: dry run, frontmatter check, quick risk warnings, symlink/submodule and
  size limits, atomic install with a backup on update, project scope, and a
  marketplace listing (default omer-yehuda/plugins).
- Default skills listing points at anthropics/skills instead of openai/skills.
- User text reaches the scripts only through a request file, never the shell.

The customs scanner (scripts/scan.js and the modules it requires), the officer
agent and the inspect/manifest skills were written by Omer Yehuda for the
Customs plugin (first released under MIT) and are included here under
Apache-2.0.

